INITIAL PLANNING 1: Object part and approach
- Object and part to interact with: the door handle lever bar, preferably near the free end (away from the spindle) to maximize torque when pressing downward.
- Which object instance to use: there is one door and one lever, so we choose the single detected handle lever.
- Approach strategy:
  - Compute unit vectors:
    - Door outward normal in XY from door angle_short (outward = −inward).
    - Door width direction in XY from door angle_long.
    - Lever long-axis direction in XY from lever angle_long.
  - Compute the lever free-end “tip” assumed along +lever_long_dir from the lever center by 0.5 × lever_length. From perception, the lever_long_dir projects strongly along the outward normal, so this tip is the one pointing outward from the door.
