- Insertion path vs. lever capture: Repeated failures point to the bar not getting inside the open jaws before closing. Pushing inward toward the door plane alone is insufficient and risks occlusion. What’s missing is a deliberate alignment scan across the lever’s thickness axis (± along angle_short) at grasp height to ensure the open pads straddle the bar before closure.
- Unlatch and pull: The press and multi-phase pull were reasonable; the failure happens earlier at the capture stage.

