- Approach vector: Approaching primarily along the door normal is fragile for lever bars mounted close to the panel. A more reliable strategy is to approach from the lever’s free tip along the lever’s long axis, then slide toward the center while staying slightly outward from the door plane until the final seating.
- User-specified yaw: The user explicitly instructed “set rotation = handle angle_long so the fingers themselves are parallel to the lever’s long axis.” We will adhere to this instruction and use θ = angle_long throughout the grasp phase.

